    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0496" n="392" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4290: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-19T12:00:00+01:00">February 19,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received February 19—8:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. The French delegation informs me that they are advised that Johnson has
                    instructions not to cooperate at Shanghai in the endeavor to arrange an
                    armistice. On the contrary the British information, though not so recent, is to
                    the effect that Johnson is cooperating. Please inform me as to facts if
                    convenient.</p>
                <p>General impression here is that efforts for the moment should be concentrated on
                    obtaining an armistice but that the distance of neutral zone, 20 kilometers,
                    demanded by the Japanese is exorbitant and Japanese should be pressed to reduce
                    it to reasonable distance, perhaps 1 kilometer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
